00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
breath of the wild to this day is still  seeing big discoveries  and chances are at some point you were  scrolling through twitter saw some wild  looking clip that made you go  huh that was cool but i have no clue  what happened oh well  and kept scrolling well my name is rin  harasaki creator of the bow spin  technique and with over 2 300 hours on  breath of the wild i'll be going over  these combat clips and breaking them  down for the average player to see  behind the scenes  so you can see just the amount of work  and difficulty that goes into this type  of gameplay  if you like these kind of intense  breakdowns let us know by subscribing  and hitting that like button so you can  break down more clips you want to see  taken apart  first let's watch the whole combat  sequence by itself without any  explanation  this amazing sequence is done by my good  friend yuda from taiwan  this clip has a lot going on under the  hood and shows how fluidly he can  perform all these advanced techniques  back to back  [Music]  all right so let's start at the  beginning we see yuda face off with the  red main lionel  and the lionel starts his charging slash  attack yuta first does a shield jump  this is a basic skill that you normally  wouldn't use in combat you normally use  it for sliding down hills  but this can be used as a quick dodge in  any direction during combat  there's also something done here under  the hood that you couldn't see with your  eyes that i'll explain in a couple  minutes  he then locks onto the lynel and then  starts doing a complex sequence  he first performs a simple bomb drop  this is the fastest way to summon a bomb  in breath of the wild by dropping it  during a jump  pulling one out and setting it down is  much slower in comparison  now comes the hard part the daruk shield  block reset  or dsbr now a regular shield  block reset is a technique in breath of  the wild that allows you to perform  bullet time  anywhere even on flat ground by blocking  an attack or bomb while jumping the hit  knocks you upwards and lets you jump a  second time  what's equivalent to a double jump in  most video games so combining this with  a backflip in this case  lets you get enough height to enter  bullet time anywhere but  the rook's shield block reset is even  harder and adds a second layer to this  try doing the same as above with the  rook's protection on it simply won't  work because the rook's protection  is getting in the way this is where it  takes a lot of skill to jump into the  attack  turn off the rook's protection by  letting go of zl blocking the attack and  backflipping to get the shield block  reset within milliseconds  to get that sought after bullet time try  it yourself it's  not easy alright now that we're airborne  yuda goes for the headshot  knocks down the lionel stunning him but  something strange happens next and link  flips his head downward all of a sudden  and goes into a strange position  this is called a thunderclap rush also  known as tcr  to perform this you have to tap the  attack and arrow shot at the same time  to confuse the game to do bullet time  and flurry rushes back to back also in  breath of the wild you've probably done  it before the standard flurry rush  it's pretty simple you dodge an attack  it goes into slow motion and then you  attack the enemy  what's actually happening is the game is  marking the target so as soon as your  feet touch the ground you will chase  after the target  this mark and chase mechanic is  constantly stored under the hood of the  game's engine every time you block  get hit or get out of a wave of attack  that's dodgeable so remember a couple  minutes ago when i told you to remember  what happened  that shield jump earlier actually marked  the target lionel to be the chase target  now that he has a lock on the lynel this  thunderclap rush uses that mark and will  chase towards the target and flurry rush  them for high damage  without marking the target it would look  like this and would be quite a  disappointment  with this technique the fact that you  can slam them with bow and arrow shots  and flurry rush right after makes this  technique have extremely high damage  capabilities  alright we're 11 seconds in still with  me here's some more  he finishes his rush and jump cancels  sideways and performs a perfect doru  crush  or pdr by dropping a bomb while jumping  detonating it and pairing it mid-air  with the rook's protection on  he's able to trick the game to think  that the bomb was an enemy attack and  force a flurry rush to happen out of  thin air  it's important to note that normally the  rook's ghost appears when you use the  rook's protection  but it does not hear that's because  there was a perfect parry using deruk's  protection  when you release or tap zl there are two  frames in dirk's protection that are  considered perfect  in a game that's 30 frames per second  two frames feels like this  you have to detonate and parry the bomb  perfectly within those two frames  with enough practice you can do it too  okay so with most of the heavy  explanations out of the way now we'll  see some repeats of previously shown  techniques  bomb drop into another daruk shio block  reset or dsbr  but instead of transferring into a  thunderclap rush like last time  we're going to do a mid-air falling  perfect deru crush with a spear  side note normal perfect daru brushes do  not chase the enemy like thunderclap  rushes  so you want to be close while doing this  or use a longer range weapon like a  spear to reach out and attack them  after the spear's flurry rush he then  does a simple technique called item hold  cancelling  link has a very slow recovery animation  after doing spear flurry rushes  so this saves precious time and forces  yourself out of that by holding an item  pretty nifty this is the final stretch  he uses stasis on the lynel and starts  charging to summon urbosa's fury  he then unleashes his attack but with  lightning quick speed switches weapons  so he doesn't have to stick around for  the whole spear charge animation  this is called the urbosa cancel the  best part is our bosa is still being  summoned after this is happening  so you can do whatever you want for half  a second before urbosa even arrives  he then uses that time to quickly switch  the bombs does one last side hop with a  perfect a root brush  with urbosa looking classy in the  background and there we go  this red main lynel was defeated in one  combo without any retaliation but  plenty of style alright time for some  homework  this will be simple homework you can do  at home for people interested in  leveling up their own combat  this one isn't nearly as complicated as  the stuff you just saw and is easy to  access early in the game and is very  useful throughout your whole playthrough  leaf bomb rolling is an easy technique  which launches your remote bombs much  farther than you ever could by just  throwing it  first find any trees and start chopping  them down until you find a korok leaf  once you have make sure to equip your  round bombs  now all you have to do is attack jump  and  drop your bomb make sure that you fully  swing first so that the gust of wind can  catch your bomb  now blow up your bomb super simple but  we can do a little bit more  [Music]  the next step up would be leaf bomb  launching and this gets a little tougher  to do  this lets you launch bombs in any  direction what you want to do is hold r  to be ready to throw while you have the  korok leaf then jump  press cell to drop your bomb and then  release r all before your feet touch  back on the ground  again it's jump press l and then release  r quickly in order if done right you'll  have to launch the bomb with the wind  and you'll have a neat projectile  [Music]  both of these are easy options that are  a neat alternative for hunting puzzling  and combat hopefully you'll have  mastered this technique by the time the  next episode drops  breath of the wild has evolved a ton  with people finding new things almost  daily since its release back in 2017  keeping this game constantly fresh so if  you found a clip recently that you want  me to break down and explain the magic  behind it  subscribe and let me know in the  comments below which one you want  explained  and also these explanations are kept  short and there are many underlying  rules to these techniques so if you want  to know more you can also look up my  combat glossary  thanks again to yuda for the footage and  go follow him because his username is  short for you who's daddy and you who is  damn adorable  and until next time take it easy  you

